# ── Never commit genomic data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This project is health *economics*; no personal genome file belongs in it. The
# rules below are precautionary, not a response to an incident — no genomic data
# has ever been committed here, and tests/test_no_genomic_data.py proves it on
# every push.
#
# Genome file formats. Deliberately no filename or sample-ID patterns here: a
# personal identifier does not belong in a public file, and the extension rules
# below plus the content scan in tests/test_no_genomic_data.py catch a raw export
# whatever it happens to be called.
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.gvcf
*.23andme

# Tabular data is opt-in, not opt-out. Raw genotype exports are plain .csv/.tsv/
# .txt, so ignore all of them and whitelist only the files this project needs.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.txt
!requirements.txt
!data/LifeTable_USA_Mx_2015.csv
